OL,3,AWho could be behind hoax bomb threats
OL,4,Ato European air travel?
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe warnings came in thick and fast,
OL,7,Ftargeting one airline or airport after
OL,8,Fanother.
OL,10,FIn nearly all cases - London's Heathrow
OL,11,Fairport being a notable exception -
OL,12,Fthey were taken to be credible enough
OL,13,Fto divert the aircraft in question, or
OL,14,Feven in Italy's case, to scramble
OL,15,Ffighter jets to escort it.
OL,17,FThey all turned out to be false, which
OL,18,Fdoes not, of course, mean that the next
OL,19,Fones will not be real.
OL,23,APub: 05-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG9/38
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
